## Command Resolution & Install Modes

Managed commands are compiled shims. Curator-managed installs prefer bare
`task-board`, `tb-sessiond`, and `task-board-tui`; otherwise resolve, in order:
`.agents/bin/<command>` (or its Windows `.cmd`), Curator `global/bin`, a bare
command verified with `command -v`/`Get-Command`, then the source-checkout
`tools/` build root. Installed Curator skills exclude build roots, and shell
profile activation is optional.

Runtime changes follow canonical `.specs/` contracts.

Spawn providers: `agy`, `claude`, `codex`, `gemini`, `muse`, `qwen`. Gemini CLI
0.54.4 is deprecated in favour of Antigravity, but both remain supported.

```bash
task-board spawn TASK-ID --role developer --background --agent agy --model gemini-3.6-flash-high --timeout 35m
```

`agy` takes no `--reasoning-effort`; effort is encoded in its eight scoped IDs:
3.1 Pro high/low and 3.5/3.6 Flash high/medium/low. Minimum `agy` is 1.1.12;
1.1.14 is validated. Version 1.1.11 exposed `--print`, `--model`, JSON output,
print timeout, accept-edits mode, skip-permissions, disable-slash-commands, and
add-dir, but is rejected. Prompt delivery has a 96 KiB argv budget; provider
print timeout is 30m and `--timeout` is the external process-tree bound.
`SUCCESS`/`ERROR` JSON overrides process exit; invalid envelopes fail and only
sanitized metadata persists. Only the top-level worker is tracked; internal
subagents and primary Session Manager support are out of scope.

```json
{"spawn":{"preferred_agentic_system":{"mixed":["agy","codex"]},"ceilings":{"agy":{"model":"gemini-3.6-flash-high","model_criterion":"equal"}},"schedule":{"windows":[{"start_utc":"17:00","end_utc":"03:00","preferred_agentic_system":{"exclusive":"agy"}}]}}}
```

`spawn.ceilings.agy` rejects `reasoning_effort`. See [README](README.md) for the
full models, flags, JSON, safety, configuration, and Gemini compatibility contract.
