# TASK-260715-whtdsf review verdict — CR revision 1

Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED. Candidate tree: 24ab4057f0ca8c62be8ec51cb540fa857048d224. Patch SHA-256: 769be0f2baa88250be99fc4313da1de867e2a9619d33f4a8e255d96e62da1c54.

## Blocking findings

1. The proposed production call site policy/board-spec is fail-open as specified. On the authoritative board, task-board validate printed [PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH] and 1 issue but returned exit 0; task-board validate --help exposes no strict flag. The current contract only says to run task-board validate, so a shell gate admits a reported invalid status. Rework must require either a validator fix or an explicit issue-count/JSON wrapper that exits nonzero, name TASK-260715-2hef52 as owner, add a real invalid-status negative fixture against the production call site, and record the anomaly. The current mismatch was induced by reviewer-state aggregation and is not itself attributed to the candidate; the fail-open exit is the defeated gate.

2. Runner scope contradicts itself. LOGBOOK.md says all pull-request and merge-queue work is GitHub-hosted macOS only. Contract section 3.2 permits native Linux relay rows, and existing ci.yml also has the non-relay validate job on ubuntu-latest. Section 3.0 incorrectly describes the seed Linux rows collectively as relay hardening. Rework must state the precise macOS working-client trust boundary, distinguish optional relay-native Linux evidence from generic policy validation, and declare future runner allocation so no Linux runner becomes a prerequisite of the working-client path.

3. Required-check cardinality drift: contract section 4 enumerates nine blocking checks, while LOGBOOK.md and TASK-260715-whtdsf_results.md claim eight. Align every binding and evidence artifact to the actual stable set.

## Passing evidence

- git diff --check for base b3422b05226253a17676b9b84c764071fe3dbe74 to candidate: exit 0.
- Candidate paths match the worktree byte-for-byte; reverse application of the exact patch: exit 0.
- PlantUML checkonly and SVG render: exit 0; regenerated SVG byte-identical.
- Every TASK owner referenced by the contract resolves on the board.
- Source authority files and existing ci.yml were readable and inspected.

## Other evidence

- task-board validate returned exit 0 while reporting one issue. This result remains failing as a gate-behavior test despite the process code.
- Product builds were not rerun because this documentation-only delta changes no executable product or workflow.
- references/negative-evidence.md remains unavailable; its content is unknown.
