   downstream owner `TASK-260715-2hef52` must implement a JSON-parsing wrapper
   that fails on invalid, malformed, unreadable, missing, or unallowlisted
   results, and must prove the same production entry point with an invalid-status
   negative fixture.
2. The existing Ubuntu generic-validation seed is distinguished from relay
   Linux work. All nine checks that block the macOS working-client path must be
   runnable on GitHub-hosted macOS; optional relay-native Linux evidence remains
   separate and cannot become a working-client prerequisite.
3. The contract, logbook, and this evidence consistently name nine stable merge
   checks.
4. A reviewer-found least-privilege contradiction is closed: the PR/fork
   `security/supply-chain` job is artifact-only and read-only; optional SARIF
   upload is isolated in trusted protected-branch `security/sarif-publish` with
   `security-reporting` approval, exact digests, one write permission, one
   endpoint, and explicit rejecting fixtures. The nine PR blocking checks are
   unchanged.

Gate A0, iOS/TestFlight/App Store workflows, workflow implementation, production
credentials, and any Linux-runner requirement for the prototype remain out of
scope. Human governance ratification remains `TASK-260717-2d308k`; publication
cannot pass before it, while downstream implementation may proceed after agent
acceptance.

