   307	### 6.2 Retention classes
   308	
   309	| Class | Content | Retention | Access/deletion |
   310	| --- | --- | --- | --- |
   311	| `diagnostic` | Redacted failed-step logs with no reusable binary | 14 days | Repository readers; automatic deletion |
   312	| `verification` | PR/test/SARIF/policy reports | 90 days | Repository readers/security as scoped; automatic deletion |
   313	| `candidate` | Unsigned/rebuilt candidate bytes and intermediate manifests | 180 days or candidate rejection + 30 days, whichever is later | Release/security; digest-indexed deletion audit |
   314	| `release-record` | Published hashes, provenance, approvals, public signing/notary/feed receipts, SBOM/notices | 7 years | Append-only release/security evidence store; deletion requires recorded policy authority |
   315	| `incident-hold` | Minimum redacted subset named by an incident | Until explicit legal/security release | Restricted; hold and deletion events audited |
   316	
   317	Retention clocks and legal-hold applicability are policy-fill decisions for
   318	later owner ratification; they do not authorize storing secrets or personal
   319	traffic data.
   320	
   321	### 6.3 Network and cache rules
   322	
   323	- Deny network by default after bootstrap. Allow only exact GitHub endpoints,
   324	  checksum-pinned package/tool origins, advisory databases, Apple notarization,
   325	  GitHub publication, and the Relux update origin in the job that owns them.
   326	- Redirects, new hosts, mutable bootstrap responses, proxy injection, or TLS
   327	  failure fail closed. Network inventories are retained in sanitized metadata.
   328	- Fork PRs may restore only read-only caches keyed by trust class, OS image,
   329	  exact tool/dependency/source hashes, and cache schema. They never save to a
   330	  namespace restored by trusted/release jobs.
   331	- Cache contents are never authoritative. Checksums, manifests, generated drift,
   332	  linkage, and artifact inspection run on every hit. Poisoned or unreadable
   333	  caches are discarded and the job rebuilds; inability to rebuild is failure.
   334	
   335	## 7. Threat and failure-path contract
   336	
   337	| Scenario | Required prevention/detection | Fail-closed result and recovery owner |
   338	| --- | --- | --- |
   339	| Forked code | No environment, secret, write token, self-hosted runner, privileged reusable workflow, or trusted cache/artifact namespace | PR remains failing; `TASK-260715-2wjvlx` fixes policy, `TASK-260715-vg2of8` proves it |
   340	| Mutable action | Full-SHA policy rejects tag/branch/range before action execution | `policy/github-actions` fails; security reviews replacement SHA |
   341	| Cache poisoning | Trust-separated keys; content verification after restore; release ignores PR caches | Discard/rebuild; verification failure blocks the owning build check |
   342	| Artifact substitution | Candidate manifest and per-file digests verified at each transfer; untrusted artifacts never promote | Consumer fails before processing; evidence owner records attempted digest mismatch |
   343	| Tag spoofing/race | Resolve once to exact protected-branch commit; validate version/tag; tag never authorizes environment | `release/candidate-identity` rejects; release owner deletes/recreates only through audited policy |
   344	| Rerun | Original candidate manifest/digests and policy revision remain fixed; attempt number is new | Changed identity creates a new candidate, not a rerun; old attempt stays non-promotable |
   345	| Cancellation/timeout/runner loss | Bounded jobs, `always()` evidence finalizer that cannot override failure, no feed publication before all receipts | Cancelled/unknown, never success; revoke temporary material and resume from last immutable receipt |
   346	| Concurrent releases | One production concurrency group, no cancel-in-progress, monotonic version reservation | Later candidate waits; conflicting version is rejected, never overwritten |
   347	| Compromised low-privilege credential | Job-specific endpoint/scope; cannot sign, alter candidate, approve environment, or delete evidence | Stop affected job, revoke/rotate, mark candidate non-promotable, security owns incident disposition |
   348	| Missing/expired credential | Preflight proves availability without printing material | Required credentialed job fails; it is never `skipped-as-pass` |
   349	| Partial publication | Versioned assets first, remote digest/header checks, signed feed atomically last | Feed withheld; exact receipts determine safe resume or withdrawal |
   350	| Scanner/advisory outage | Distinguish no findings from unavailable database/service | `unknown` blocks `security/supply-chain`; security owner decides only through audited exception |
   351	| Evidence/log upload failure | Gate result and evidence persistence are both required | Owning check fails even when build/tests passed |
   352	
   353	No workflow may convert failure into success with `continue-on-error`, blanket
   354	retry, fallback credentials, alternate unsigned feed/download, stale evidence,
   355	or a summary-only aggregator. Matrix aggregation reports every child result and
   356	fails unless all required children succeeded.
   357	
